>> title: Skillet Lasagna
>> category: Pasta
>> tags: pasta, sausage, tomatoes, one-pot, skillet, weeknight
>> counters: One Pot
>> aka: one-pan lasagna, lazy lasagna, broken lasagna, skillet lasagne
>> servings: 4
>> time: 50 min
>> step.1: The noodles go in dry and broken, and they cook in the sauce rather than in a pot of water beside it. That is the whole trade: no layers, no baking dish, no colander, and the starch the noodles shed is what thickens the sauce instead of going down the drain.
>> step.2: brown 8 min, broken up
>> step.3: soften 4 min
>> step.4: simmer covered 20 min, noodles under the sauce
>> step.5: dot with cheese, stand covered 5 min
>> step.6: Push the noodles under the liquid before the lid goes on and stir once at the ten-minute mark, or the pieces on top come out leathery at the edges. If it tightens before they are tender, another splash of water; the sauce should be loose when the cheese goes on and right by the time it melts.

The noodles go in dry and broken, and they cook in the sauce rather than in a pot of water beside it. That is the whole trade: no layers, no baking dish, no colander, and the starch the noodles shed is what thickens the sauce instead of going down the drain.

Brown @Italian sausage{1%lb}(450 g; casings off) in @olive oil{1%Tbs} in a #cast-iron skillet{} for ~brown{8%min}.

Soften @&(~1)sausage{} with @yellow onion{1%medium}(diced), @garlic{4%cloves}(sliced), @dried oregano{1%tsp}, @red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp} for ~saute{4%min}.

Simmer @&(~1)base{} covered with @canned crushed tomatoes{28%oz}(800 g), @water{1 1/2%cups}(360 mL), @lasagna noodles{8%oz}(225 g; broken in 2-in pieces), @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} for ~simmer{20%min}.

Dot @&(~1)skillet lasagna{} with @whole-milk ricotta{1%cup}(250 g), @low-moisture mozzarella{1%cup}(115 g; shredded), @basil{1/4%cup}(torn) and ~stand{5%min} covered off the heat.

Push the noodles under the liquid before the lid goes on and stir once at the ten-minute mark, or the pieces on top come out leathery at the edges. If it tightens before they are tender, another splash of water; the sauce should be loose when the cheese goes on and right by the time it melts.
